  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Minobasco (Shokoba). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Minobasco (often associated with the name 'Shokoba') is a specialized, modern variant of the traditional Italian fishing game 'Escoba' (or Scopa). It is unique for its use of colorful plastic 'Gemstones' as scoring tokens and its simplified point-capture rules aimed at a faster, more competitive pace. Like Scopa, players use cards from their hand to capture sums of cards from the table, but with an emphasis on 'Shokoba'â€”clearing the entire table for a bonus point.",
    objective: 'Score Gemstones by capturing table cards (by matching value or sum), by making a Shokoba (sweep) when you clear the table, and from end-of-round awards (most cards, most Coins/Diamonds, Settebello, Primiera). The first player or team to reach 11 Gemstones wins the game.',
    gameplay: "1. **Capture**: Play a card from your hand. If its value matches a single card or the SUM of multiple cards on the table, you capture them.\n2. **Example**: A player plays a 7; they can take a 7 from the table, or a 4 and a 3, or a 5 and a 2.\n3. **Shokoba!**: If you capture ALL remaining cards on the table, you shout 'SHOKOBA!' and win 1 Gemstone immediately.",
    keyRules: [
      'Capture by playing a card that matches one table card or the sum of several table cards; if both match, take the single card.',
      'When a capture is possible you must capture.',
      'Shokoba: clearing the entire table in one play scores 1 Gemstone.',
      'First to 11 Gemstones wins.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
